@host = http://localhost:5203
@issuer = http://localhost:8080/default

### No token required.
GET {{host}}/api/public

### What the SPA reads before anyone has signed in.
GET {{host}}/api/app

# ───────────────────────── local password login ─────────────────────────

### Register. Only mapped because LocalLogin:AllowSelfRegistration is true.
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userName": "pianonic", "email": "nic@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery" }

### Log in. The identifier is a user name or an email address.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "nic@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery" }

@token = paste-the-accessToken-here
@refresh = paste-the-refreshToken-here

### The locally issued token works on the same endpoints an identity provider's token does.
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Wrong password, unknown user and a locked account are one answer. Try all three.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "nobody-at-all", "password": "correct horse battery" }

### Rotate. The presented token is dead afterwards.
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### Present the OLD refresh token again: reuse, and the whole family is revoked. Watch the log.
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### Change the password. Ends every other session.
POST {{host}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "currentPassword": "correct horse battery", "newPassword": "a whole new password" }

### Add a password to an account that arrived through the identity provider: no current password.
POST {{host}}/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "currentPassword": null, "newPassword": "a whole new password" }

### Always 204, whether the address is known, unknown, or belongs to an SSO-only account.
POST {{host}}/auth/password/forgot
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nic@example.com" }

### The token is written to the log by the sample's notifier. Paste it here.
POST {{host}}/auth/password/reset
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste-the-token-from-the-log", "newPassword": "a whole new password" }

### Revokes the family.
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

# ───────────────────────── two-factor authentication ─────────────────────────

### Nothing enrolled yet.
GET {{host}}/auth/2fa
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A password-only token is refused here: the policy wants amr to contain mfa.
GET {{host}}/api/sensitive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Begin. Returns the secret and an otpauth:// URI - scan it, or type the secret in by hand.
### Nothing is enabled yet, and signing in is unchanged until the next request succeeds.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/begin
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Confirm with the code your authenticator is showing. Returns the recovery codes, once.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "code": "000000" }

### Now log in again: 200, but with a challenge and no tokens.
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "nic@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery" }

@challenge = paste-the-challenge-here

### The challenge is not a bearer token. This is 401, and cannot be configured into working.
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{challenge}}

### Finish the sign-in. "code" takes a TOTP code or a recovery code - either shape works.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challenge": "{{challenge}}", "code": "000000" }

@mfaToken = paste-the-new-accessToken-here

### That token carries amr ["pwd","otp","mfa"], so the policy lets it through.
GET {{host}}/api/sensitive
Authorization: Bearer {{mfaToken}}

### Present the same challenge again: 401. It was spent the moment it worked.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challenge": "{{challenge}}", "code": "000000" }

### New codes, invalidating every previous one. Needs proof, same as disabling.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/recovery-codes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{mfaToken}}

{ "proof": "000000" }

### Disabling needs a current code too: an authenticated session alone is not enough.
POST {{host}}/auth/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{mfaToken}}

{ "proof": "000000" }

# ───────────────────────── identity provider ─────────────────────────

### Mint a token from the mock issuer. Copy access_token into @idpToken below.
POST {{issuer}}/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=toamaisutaa-sample&client_secret=whatever&scope=openid profile email roles

@idpToken = paste-the-access-token-here

### Same endpoint, same pipeline, different issuer.
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{idpToken}}

### Requires the role named by Oidc:AdminRole. The IdP token carries it; a local token does not.
GET {{host}}/api/admin
Authorization: Bearer {{idpToken}}

### Without a token: 401.
GET {{host}}/api/me
